# A bare path and its splat are separate rules and fail independently - the same
# reason public/_redirects lists "/admin" and "/admin/*" as two entries. Without
# the bare rule, /admin fell through to the host default of
# "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate", which lets the browser store the shell
# and re-serve it on a 304. Every deploy renames every asset, so a shell that
# outlives its deploy points at files that 404 - a white page with "Refused to
# apply style ... MIME type text/html". Caught by `npm run check:deploy`.
/admin
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  Pragma: no-cache
  Expires: 0
  CDN-Cache-Control: no-store
  Clear-Site-Data: "cache"

/admin/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate
  Pragma: no-cache
